GCC-backend port of the fork's C++ vtable machinery (LLVM
cxx_vtable.rs, Itanium half). rustc -Zcodegen-backend=gcc now emits
_ZTV/_ZTI/_ZTS for #[repr(cpp)] classes and installs the vptr in
constructors, so a pure-GCC pipeline (cg_gcc Rust + g++ C++) does
cross-language virtual dispatch in both directions.

gccjit specifics vs the LLVM emission:
- vague linkage: gccjit has no linkonce_odr/comdat — globals are
  emitted Exported plus a top-level-asm '.weak <sym>' directive
  (ELF targets; the GCC phase targets Linux).
- emission timing: queued during predefine_fn, flushed AFTER the
  predefine loop (base.rs) — eager emission would get_fn_addr
  methods that aren't predefined yet, creating imported gccjit
  functions that can never become definitions.
- constant address points (&_ZTV[2], RTTI vtable + 2 slots) use the
  new_array_access(..).get_address(..) constant form on u8-typed
  bases — void* bases ICE GCC (incomplete element type) and
  struct-typed bases would stride struct-sized.
- the deleting-dtor thunk (drop_in_place + _ZdlPv) is an ordinary
  gccjit function; vptr stores cast the return place to (u8*)*.
- abi.rs: the fork's CanonAbi::Cpp/Swift map to plain C at the GCC
  level (Itanium member fns are C functions with this first; Swift
  interop stays LLVM-only).

Probe (container, x86_64-linux, CI libgccjit + g++ 13):
  class Widget + class Gauge : Widget, -Zcodegen-backend=gcc:
  make_widget_value(5)=105 (Rust path, vptr install),
  placement-new Widget(7)->foo()=107 (C++ ctor call + dispatch
  through the Rust-emitted vtable),
  init_gauge(3,4) as Widget* ->foo()=4000 (override via derived
  vtable, indirect) — PASS.
